  "body": "**Scoped corollary (obstruction) with exact finite checks; no \u03ba change.** Bit track, card `bit-new-register-model`, seed 9.\n\nPR288 (eumemic) studies the bit primitive in its superposition register model, where gates may join registers at different frames.\n- Its theorem `G\u2080` shows that free Levi maps applied in the middle of the network never save at `m = 2`.\n- Its open item 3 is the full nonabelian Borel model, with the natively free lower-left updates `D += K\u00b7H` (upstream Lemma `ordered-affine-streams`).\n\nThis package writes out the `p = 2` instance of PR288's own first-order tool on `\u039b/p\u039b` (\u00a71.1(a), \u00a71.4(a)) for that full lower Borel, using P1's `\u03bd(g) = len(im g_HD)` read through the mod-2 natural representation. Suppose every *applied* matrix is 2-integral; inverses need not be. Then:\n\n    \u03a3_paid rank_Q A  \u2265  \u03a3_w rank_F2((g_w mod 2)_HD)  =  mW   on unit targets.\n\nSo on unit targets the bill is `(1/W) \u03a3 n_r (r/m)^{1\u2212a} \u2265 1`, with no saving at any width, register count or auxiliary count.\n\n**On unit targets, PR288's open item 3 is therefore open only where data outside `Z_(2)` is needed.** That covers:\n- dyadic paid frames;\n- applied free maps with even denominators;\n- 2-integral words on targets that are not units mod 2, such as `n_{2I} = d\u00b7n_I\u00b7d\u207b\u00b9` with `d = diag(2I, I)`. These get only the weaker bound `\u03a3 rank (g_w mod 2)_HD`.\n\nFollowing PR288 \u00a71.3(b) and PR2110, only the data\u2013data block is constrained. Beyond specialising PR288's tool, the package adds:\n- applied free maps may be singular mod 2, such as `diag(2I, I)`, because the argument runs over the monoid algebra;\n- a remark for `m = 1` with any rational data, via a mod-`p` permutation module. It is only a sanity bound: PR288's flag theorem already covers `m = 1` without `D += K\u00b7H`.\n\nThe 2-integral hypothesis is needed in general. Upstream Prop. `bit-motif-interface` is an XOR network on shear frames with `s_b < W_b m`, and by P1 Cor. alg-mixed(ii) such a network must use an even denominator. The first open case is therefore `m = 2` with `D += K\u00b7H` and data outside `Z_(2)`.\n\n**Reproduce** (standard library, exact arithmetic):\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/bit-full-borel-2adic-floor/verify.py              # ~6 s\n# PASS_BIT_FULL_BOREL_2ADIC_FLOOR_FINITE_CHECKS products=90 cancellations=18 words=96 steps=864 singular_free=74 direct=4 conjugated=2 borel=2 general_targets=3 width_one_steps=384 scope_controls=4\npython3 -I -B research/bit-full-borel-2adic-floor/verify.py --mutations  # ~15 s\n# PASS_BIT_FULL_BOREL_2ADIC_FLOOR_MUTATIONS rejected=8/8\n```\nThese are finite sanity checks of the lemmas, not the proof:\n- `\u03c0` is multiplicative on exact group-algebra products, including forced F2 cancellations;\n- `\u03c1` is subadditive and zero on free moves, including maps singular mod 2;\n- `\u03c1` is at most `rank A` per paid call along random words with auxiliaries;\n- 8 positive controls reach the target exactly at cost `mW`: direct words, Levi-conjugated words, and Borel-conjugated words with `K \u2260 0`;\n- data-block controls;\n- the `m = 1` module on dyadic words;\n- scope controls.\n\nA shipped `--mutations` mode injects 8 defects and requires each to be rejected. The receipt is pinned, and `research_package.py --check-only` and the research unit tests pass. The runs used CPython 3.14.4; the registered 3.12 replay was not run.\n\n**Credits.**\n- Swapnil Jain, P1 (doi:10.5281/zenodo.23265442): `\u03bd` and Theorem A, Interface I, Cor. alg-mixed(ii), Prop. alg-origin.\n- eumemic, PR288: the superposition model, the FO lemma and its `\u039b/p\u039b` form, the data-block use, the permutation-module certificates, `G\u2080` and item 3.\n- Cinna Davis: PR2110, PR2085, PR2112.\n- Gareth Davidson: PR1333.\n- Tuafo and Maximooch: PR1604 and PR1679.\n- philippeVV: Discussion 1587.\n- The upstream authors.\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5). Four rounds of adversarial AI review (eight reviewers) shaped the scope and credits. The main correction was that the core is PR288's own FO-on-`\u039b/p\u039b` tool, so the note is positioned as a corollary; no independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
